# Elixir sources are checked in with LF endings.
#
# 27 files under elixir/ were committed with CRLF. Elixir 1.20's formatter
# tolerates that; the 1.15 the CI gate pins does not, and reported all 26 of
# them (every one that .formatter.exs globs) as unformatted -- so
# `mix format --check-formatted` could not pass on CI and did pass locally, on
# the same bytes.
#
# Scoped deliberately. CRLF is repo-wide -- hundreds of tracked files across Go,
# TypeScript, Python, Zig, Julia, Quint and the docs -- but no other gate
# enforces line endings, and `* text=auto` would renormalize the whole tree on
# everyone's next checkout. Widening this is a separate decision, not a
# side effect of greening a gate.
*.ex  text eol=lf
*.exs text eol=lf
